SPECIALIST PLAN:
Plan: Find and visit two objects in order: 1) container, 2) rock. Roles and sequence:

Navigator:
- Drive Q1 to successive stationary goals only when ordered by planner. Goals will be either: (A) an approach pose computed from a sensed object centroid (never the centroid itself; at least 3 m from the centroid toward the robot) or (B) a free occupancy-cell chosen to explore when the current target class is not yet detected. Always stop and hold at each goal; do not move while lidar/camera sense or confirm.
- After stopping at each ordered stop, wait for a confirm_stop(name) from lidar or camera before proceeding.

Lidar:
- When Q1 is stationary, run semantic lidar scans. If an object of interest (container or rock) is detected, report its class and centroid x/y.
- When the navigator has stopped at an approach pose for the current target class, call confirm_stop(name) for that class (where name is the class string ‘container’ or ‘rock’) to verify the stop. If confirm_stop fails, report and continue sensing; request a new approach pose from planner.

Camera:
- When Q1 is stationary, capture an RGB image (and optional class histogram) to aid confirmation. If lidar cannot confirm a stop, attempt confirm_stop(name) using the camera.

Procedure / decision rules:
1) Start: both lidar and camera sense in place.
2) If lidar reports target class with centroid, planner computes an approach goal at least 3 m from centroid toward current robot pose, instruct navigator to go there and stop.
3) After stop, lidar (preferred) calls confirm_stop(name). If lidar cannot confirm after reasonable sensing, camera attempts confirm_stop(name). Only when confirm_stop(name) returns true do we mark that target visited and proceed to the next target class.
4) If target class is not detected by lidar while stationary, planner will request occupancy map and pick a free cell in a different quadrant from any already-seen objects; navigator will drive there and repeat sensing.
5) Repeat sense → move → sense until both container and rock are confirmed visited. Never navigate to any object centroid and always maintain >=3 m distance.

All specialists: report failures or detection events back to planner so the planner can compute approach poses or select alternative explore cells.

